<title>USA: YPF SA renews Canadon Seco contract with Brazil.</title>
<headline>YPF SA renews Canadon Seco contract with Brazil.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine YPF SA renewed a term contract for Canadon Seco last week with Brazil's state oil company Petrobras, sources said Tuesday.</p>
<p>The six month contract for 15,000 barrels per day (bpd) starting in October was renewed at a price of $2.45 a barrel (fob) below the marker West Texas Intermediate.</p>
<p>Previously, the contract price was WTI minus $2.66 a barrel, traders said.</p>
<p>YPF SA also signed two similar contracts for 15,000 bpd starting next month at WTI minus $2.00 a barrel, but the price includes the cost of lightering.</p>
<p>The contracts were likely signed by a trader and a U.S. refiner, sources said.</p>
<p>--Jacqueline Wong, New York Energy Desk +1 212 859 1620</p>
